Hi both,

https://github.com/tessera-io/platform/pull/512

This is the first half of the Northstar SAP connector: a parser for DELVRY03 IDocs that is driven entirely by the field-mapping table Hana is producing with the Fresno planners. The parser itself knows nothing about Northstar; every field name, unit and default lives in connectors/sap/mappings/northstar-fresno.yaml, so a second plant is a second file.

Please read in this order:
1. connectors/sap/mapping_loader.py - validates the table against the IDoc segment schema at load time, so a typo in the mapping fails at startup instead of at 02:00 on cutover night.
2. connectors/sap/idoc.py - the segment iterator. It streams; a 40 MB IDoc batch does not get loaded into memory.
3. tests/connectors/sap/ - 31 fixtures from Northstar's sandbox, including the two malformed ones their team sent us on purpose.

WHSCON is a follow-up PR; the loader is shared. Runbook page for operators is drafted: https://runbooks.tessera.io/connectors/sap-idoc

It is ~900 lines with tests, so take your time; I would like it merged by Thursday so Carmen can point the regression suite at it.

Thanks,

Arjun
